    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "can u summarize the main steps a company needs to follow if a user submits a formal request to be forgotten under gdpr? need to make sure our internal memo is accurate.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If a user submits a formal request to be forgotten under GDPR, a company typically follows these steps:\n\n1. Acknowledge the request and inform the user of the data processing activities they are subject to, as well as their rights under the GDPR.\n2. Provide evidence that processing is necessary, and the processing data subject is the one requesting erasure.\n3. Immediately erase the personal data from the company's servers, unless GDPR exceptions apply.\n4. Issue a confirmation of erasure to the user, usually in writing, once the erasure is complete.\n\nNote that this can be done through an email or an external link, which documents the deletion of the data.",
